WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.479
ALEX: So here is what OpenAI actually
announced. Employees can flag possible
model-misalignment

00:00:04.479 --> 00:00:08.958
ALEX: incidents. Those go to safety and
alignment teams for investigation. Those
teams

00:00:08.958 --> 00:00:13.438
ALEX: then decide whether the case
should be publicly disclosed. Reuters
reported it

00:00:13.438 --> 00:00:17.917
ALEX: on September 16, 2026.

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:19.221
JAMIE: That's where I stop.

00:00:19.291 --> 00:00:20.489
ALEX: Why there specifically?

00:00:20.589 --> 00:00:24.343
JAMIE: Because "warrants" is a judgment
call made by the people whose valuation

00:00:24.343 --> 00:00:28.097
JAMIE: depends on the answer. There is
no external check on that decision.

00:00:28.097 --> 00:00:31.852
JAMIE: An employee flags something.
OpenAI's own safety team reviews it.
OpenAI then

00:00:31.852 --> 00:00:35.606
JAMIE: decides if the public gets to
know. That's one organization
controlling the

00:00:35.606 --> 00:00:39.360
JAMIE: entire chain.
